-  "publication_date": "2026-06-13",
-  "description": "<p>Dedicated Gordan / Clebsch-Gordan working-edition record for the Modern LaTeX Editions of Mathematics Manuscripts project. This record holds source-witnessed LaTeX and English translation working drafts, scans, and audit ledgers for Gordan/Clebsch-Gordan material.</p><p><strong>Current public surface.</strong> The current record carries the completed authorial text of <em>Theorie der Abelschen Functionen</em> through <code>Gordan_Abel27_p343_355_DE_EN_20260612.zip</code>, the recursive Abelsche final-audit/fix package <code>Gordan_Abelsche_FinalAuditFix02_DE_EN_20260613.zip</code>, the Latin/English <em>De linea geodetica</em> p001-p047 package, the theta 1863 full-audit fix06 package, and the first two <em>Vorlesungen ueber Invariantentheorie</em> Bd. 1 tranches <code>Gordan_VB1_01_p001_009_DE_EN_20260613.zip</code> and <code>Gordan_VB1_02_p010_028_DE_EN_20260613.zip</code>. This makes the Abelsche final-audit layer, De linea p001-p047, theta fix06, and Vorlesungen Bd.1 p001-p028 public.</p><p><strong>Status at a glance.</strong> Earlier Abel tranches and AllPrior/AuditFix packets remain correction/provenance layers. The full Gordan article corpus register remains open, and <em>Vorlesungen</em> Bd.1 is only begun through source p28.</p><p><strong>Quality note.</strong> These are package-audited, source-witnessed working drafts and source-audit packets, not certified critical editions. Scans and zoom crops control mathematical readings; OCR scaffolds are non-authoritative locator/comparison witnesses only. Verify important formulas, diagrams, notation, and theorem statements against the included source witnesses.</p><p><strong>Corrections and collaboration.</strong> Source comparisons, LaTeX fixes, translation corrections, and reader-facing issue reports can be suggested through GitHub issues or pull requests: <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
+  "title": "Paul Gordan and Clebsch-Gordan: Working Editions and Source-Witnessed LaTeX",
+  "publication_date": "2026-08-11",
+  "description": "<p>Start here: <code>00_CURRENT_Gordan_Vorlesungen_I-II_German_FirstPass_20260811.pdf</code> is a single 455-page reader containing both volumes of Paul Gordan's <em>Vorlesungen &uuml;ber Invariantentheorie</em>. The two per-volume PDFs and compact buildable-TeX archives follow it.</p><p><strong>New milestone (2026-08-11).</strong> Band I (<em>Determinanten</em>) has 206 German fragments covering frozen source indices 15&ndash;220 and printed pages 1&ndash;201; its reader has 159 pages. Band II (<em>Bin&auml;re Formen</em>) has 362 German fragments covering source indices 15&ndash;376 and printed pages 1&ndash;360; its reader has 296 pages. Both assemble and compile in two passes. The release status and checksum manifest record the source scans, corpus fingerprints, collector results, build diagnostics, cold rebuild, and rendered QA.</p><p><strong>Scope boundary.</strong> This is a complete compiling first-pass German transcription of these two books. It is not a canonical or critical collation, not a bilingual edition, and not completion of Paul Gordan's author corpus. There are zero English fragments. Eighty-eight explicit uncertainty markers remain (38 in Band I and 50 in Band II), together with four textual figure or ornament stand-ins (three plus one). These are published visibly so later source replay can improve the witness without concealing the present state.</p><p>The 45 predecessor files remain part of this version as provenance and as source-witnessed working packages for other Gordan/Clebsch-Gordan works. The new <em>Vorlesungen</em> files supersede the June statement that Band I stopped at page 28 and Band II had not started; they do not supersede unrelated Abelian, theta, Latin, or article material.</p><p><strong>Editorial method.</strong> Printed scan pixels control the German witness. Explicit uncertainties, source defects, and figure gaps are preserved rather than guessed. Important formulae and notation should still be checked against the named 600-ppi GDZ source scans. Further work consists of bounded source replay, figure restoration, and a separate future English lane.</p><p>Corrections may be proposed through <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
